Debian package for the llama PHP extension.

`dpkg-buildpackage` builds `php-llama` against every PHP version
`phpquery -V` reports (on these suites that is the distro default,
via `php-all-dev`). `dh-php` installs:

  /usr/lib/php/<api>/llama.so
  /etc/php/<version>/mods-available/llama.ini

and the maintainer scripts call `php_invoke enmod <version> ALL llama`.
That is the same hook packaged PHP modules use: it registers the module
and enables it for every SAPI of that version (`cli`, `fpm`, `apache2`,
and the rest). A SAPI package installed afterwards enables registered
modules itself, so fpm or apache added later still loads llama.

Build (amd64), after `./scripts/fetch-libllama.sh`:

  sudo apt-get install -y build-essential dpkg-dev debhelper dh-php php-all-dev pkgconf
  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b

GitHub Actions does this per suite and appends `+<suite>` to the Debian
version so trixie, plucky, questing, and resolute do not share one pool
filename. `scripts/release.sh` tags; it does not build the packages.
